# Layer 1 (local, fast feedback) of the CI/Husky mandate for frontend
# templates — hefesto's ADR 0026 / .claude/rules/frontend-template-baseline.md
# extends the same shape ADR 0014/0026 already establish for backend
# templates (see `express-ts`'s repo-root pre-commit hook in
# `colidevs/create-coliapp`). Kept fast and pre-commit-appropriate: lint +
# format check, type check, then Vitest — which now runs both the `node`
# unit-test project (Phase 2) and the `storybook` component-test project
# (Phase 4, @storybook/addon-vitest, vitest.config.mts) from one `pnpm test`
# invocation. E2E (Playwright) and Lighthouse CI are deliberately NOT run
# here — both start a real dev/prod server and are too slow for a
# pre-commit hook; they run in CI (`.github/workflows/frontend-standard.yml`)
# instead.
#
# One-time local setup this hook assumes: `pnpm exec playwright install
# chromium` (the `storybook` Vitest project needs a real Chromium install,
# same as CI's own explicit install step).
pnpm exec biome check . || exit 1
pnpm exec tsc --noEmit || exit 1
pnpm test || exit 1
